  "limitations": "Astronomical year zero exists; negative years are not historical BC labels. Valid range -4799..9999, strict month/day and Gregorian leap-year rules; no adoption-date switch, business days, holidays, timezone, UTC leap seconds or UTC/TT/UT1 conversion. Distinct from the existing financial day-count/business-calendar pack. Keep the two parts for downstream precision rather than assuming the summed JD preserves fine time resolution.",
  "port_notes": "Ports eraCal2jd integer arithmetic, including truncation-toward-zero for (month-14)/12. The rest of the dividends are nonnegative in the admitted domain. Unlike ERFA status -3, this adapter rejects an invalid day rather than returning a computed JD alongside an error status. Caps the otherwise broader upper-year range at 9999. Full ERFA BSD license and source SOFA-heritage notice are retained; this is an ERFA-derived adaptation, not an official SOFA distribution.",
